// TEST: Quantity Slot Rejects Structural Argument (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3010
// Matching DIMENSIONS do not imply the quantity: a Float<mps> value is
// rejected by a Float<speed> parameter until the caller ascribes it
// (`twice((m : speed))`). The dims agree perfectly; what is missing is the
// caller's assertion.
Unit meters
Unit seconds
Unit mps = meters / seconds
Unit speed: mps
function twice(x: Float<speed>) -> Float<speed> = x + x
let m: Float<mps> = 4.0
let r = twice(m)
